        "notes": "Line 1 (passes: 1, MAR author sourcing, 2026-10-30): the claims are that 비빔밥 is rice mixed with vegetables, 나물, meat and seasoning; that at home it is often mixed before it is put into the bowls; and that in a restaurant the toppings are set on the rice and each person mixes their own. National Folk Museum of Korea, 한류문화사전 entry 비빔밥 (topic 12006, HTTP 200): 정의 lists 채소·나물·반찬·고기·양념 mixed into rice; 내용 names two ways, mixing first and topping the bowls (the home way) and setting the ingredients on the rice for the eater to mix (the way the city restaurants of the 1900s served it), and calls the first 가정식 and the second 음식점 판매용. Standard Korean Language Dictionary, 비빔-밥 (HTTP 200): rice eaten mixed with meat or 나물 and seasonings. Line 2 (passes: 2, MAR culture and facts checker, 2026-10-30): both pages fetched again: confirmed. 'Often' keeps the home sentence from reading as a rule for every home; the restaurant sentence restates 음식점 판매용 and names no restaurant, city or brand (the entry's Jeonju, airline and celebrity passages are left out on purpose). Named as of the access date. Line 3 (passes: 3, MAR third pass after the reviser, 2026-10-30): re-read; the English copies no run of words, and the ko text says it in its own words (reworded after the independent review, 2026-10-31); the es and ko texts keep both {ko:} tokens and the hedge (muchas veces; 때가 많아요)."
