        "notes": "Line 1 (passes: 1, MAR author sourcing, 2026-10-30): the claims are that the first known written recipe for 비빔밥 is in a cookbook handwritten in Hangul in the late 1800s, and that it mixes rice with stir-fried meat, 나물 and sesame oil, then lays pieces of fried egg on top. National Folk Museum of Korea, 한국의식주생활사전 entry 비빔밥 (topic 7703, HTTP 200), 내용: the recipe first appears in 『시의전서』, a Hangul manuscript written around the late 19th century; it mixes the rice with stir-fried meat, 간납, several 나물 and crushed 튀각, with sesame salt and plenty of sesame oil, and lays fried egg cut into pieces on top. The 한류문화사전 entry (topic 12006) also dates the recipes it reads to cookbooks of the late 19th and early 20th centuries. Line 2 (passes: 2, MAR culture and facts checker, 2026-10-30): both entries fetched again: confirmed. 'First known' restates 처음으로 나온다 (first appears) without claiming the dish began then; 'handwritten' restates 필사본. The note does not name the book, so no title is romanized; it lists three of the ingredients and says nothing of the others. Named as of the access date. Line 3 (passes: 3, MAR third pass after the reviser, 2026-10-30): re-read; the English copies no run of words; es and ko keep the two {ko:} tokens and the late-1800s date (a finales del siglo XIX; 1800년대 말)."
